{
    "background_story": "Yael was a renowned painter known for her strict adherence to formalism. She believed that art should be governed by a set of strict rules and principles, rather than emotional expression. Her studio was a shrine to precision, with every brushstroke and color choice carefully calculated. Yael's paintings were characterized by their geometric shapes, clean lines, and muted palette. Critics praised her work for its intellectual rigor and technical mastery. Despite the temptation to experiment with more expressive styles, Yael remained committed to her formalist ideals, even when they fell out of favor with the art world. Her dedication earned her a reputation as a true original, and her work continues to be celebrated for its innovative use of traditional techniques.",
